{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce a specific headlamp glare assessment into the MOT test",
        "additional_details": "Existing MOT requirements include checks relating to headlamp condition and alignment. However, we want an additional assessment specifically addressing excessive glare from dipped headlights.\r\n\r\nThis petition does not seek to ban LED headlights, regulate bulb wattage or restrict a particular lighting technology. It asks for the effect of dipped headlights on other road users to be specifically assessed as part of the MOT.",
        "background": "We want the Government to introduce an additional MOT assessment specifically designed to identify dipped headlights that cause excessive glare to other road users. This should be separate from existing headlamp aim and condition requirements and apply regardless of the lighting technology used.",
